WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.000
- [Instructor] Let's say we
wanna figure out what 473

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.390
divided by five is.

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:09.550
And like always, why
don't you pause this video

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:10.760
and try to work through it?

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:12.270
And if you're familiar with the idea

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:14.810
of division with partial quotients,

00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:16.863
I encourage you to try it out that way.

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:19.860
All right, now let's
work on this together.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.520
And so let me just
rewrite this in a format

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:24.120
that makes it a little bit easier for me

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:27.220
to do my division with partial quotients.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:29.453
And so I'm just going to write 473

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:34.123
divided by five.

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:39.330
And what's neat about division
with partial quotients is

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:41.590
that there's a lot of
flexibility in how you do it.

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:43.870
There's no exactly one right way.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:45.360
And so you could say, all right,

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:48.230
how many times can five go into 473

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:51.150
without going over 473?

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:52.030
You might be tempted.

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:53.980
Someone might say, "Oh, maybe
you can go a hundred times."

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:56.810
But you could quickly see that
if you said a hundred times,

00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:58.450
and they say, "How much do I left over?"

00:00:58.450 --> 00:00:59.647
you do a hundred times five.

00:00:59.647 --> 00:01:01.160
You get 500.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:04.350
And you'd say, "Oh, wait,
wait, I overshot 473."

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:06.560
So a hundred is too high.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:08.460
So then you would back up a little bit.

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:09.307
And then you could say,

00:01:09.307 --> 00:01:11.827
"All right, I'm gonna go for low numbers

00:01:11.827 --> 00:01:14.360
"and just slowly chip away at it."

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:17.050
So you might say that five goes into 473.

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:19.220
You know it goes more than 20 times.

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:21.310
Let's just start with 20.

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:23.590
Well, what is 20 times five?

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:27.220
20 times five is 100.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:28.880
And let me be very clear what that is.

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:33.350
That is 20 times our
five right over there.

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:36.160
And so clearly we did not overshoot it,

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:40.300
but how many more times can
five go into 473 than 20?

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.360
To figure that out,

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:44.600
we figure out how much more
we have left over to go,

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:47.790
so we subtract the hundred from 473.

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:51.330
And we have 373.

00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:54.710
So how many times can five go into 373?

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:59.670
Well, if 20 times five was a hundred,

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:01.450
well, gee, this is 300 here.

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:03.650
So maybe we can go another 60 times.

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:06.570
So let me put a 60 right over there.

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:09.360
And so what is 60 times five?

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:14.330
Well, six 10s times five
would be 30 10s, which is 300.

00:02:14.330 --> 00:02:17.780
And so how much further do we have to go?

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:21.510
So we still have 73 left.

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:25.900
373 minus 300 is 73.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:30.060
So how many times does five go into 73?

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:31.480
Well, let's see.

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:35.980
I know five times 12 is
60, so let me try a 12.

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:38.950
So I'll put a 12 over here.

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:42.110
And so 12 times five is 60,

00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:45.284
so how much further do we have to go?

00:02:45.284 --> 00:02:48.150
Let's see, 73 minus 60 is 13.

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:49.910
And five can go into 13,

00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:52.430
so we can get a few more fives in there.

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:53.420
Just to be clear what we're doing,

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:55.210
we've already said,
hey, we can go 20 times

00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:58.510
and then another 60 and
then another 12 times.

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:01.150
And if we go into 473 all of those times,

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:02.960
we still have 13 left over.

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:04.140
So we could go into,

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:06.500
we can even fit a few more fives in there.

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:08.480
Now, how many times does five go into 13?

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:09.770
Well, five times two is 10.

00:03:09.770 --> 00:03:11.470
Five times three would be too much.

00:03:11.470 --> 00:03:13.410
So we could say two times.

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:16.540
So that gets us two times five is 10.

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:20.750
And so there what we have
left over is a three.

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:22.830
And then we can't fit any more fives in.

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:25.010
We can't divide five into three,

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:26.930
so that's going to give us our remainder.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:30.700
So how many times does five go into 473?

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:33.250
Well, we were able to
get it in there 20 times

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:36.560
and then another 60 times
and then another 12 times

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:38.270
and then another two times.

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:41.330
So what we can do is we can
add all of these together,

00:03:41.330 --> 00:03:42.163
and what do we get?

00:03:42.163 --> 00:03:45.520
Two times plus 12 is 14,

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:50.153
plus 60 is 74, plus 20 is 94.

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:53.550
And then we have a remainder of three.

00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:56.340
So this is equal to 94,

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:58.840
and then I'll write this in
red, with a remainder of three.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:03:59.800
Did I do that right?

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:01.630
Two plus 14, let's see.

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:03.530
Two plus 12 is 14.

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:05.310
74, yeah, 94.

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:06.810
Now let me just show you that there's more

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:08.300
than one way to do this.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:09.420
I'll draw a little line here

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:11.510
so we don't get it too confused.

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:15.040
We could have done something like this.

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:18.490
We could've said what is 473

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:21.810
divided by five?

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:25.260
And we might've immediately
recognized that,

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:28.500
all right, five goes into 40 eight times.

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:32.930
So five would go into
400 80 times at least,

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:36.320
probably more times than that,
but let's just start with 80.

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:40.060
And so how close does that get us to 473?

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:40.920
Well, to figure that out,

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:44.970
we multiply 80 times five to get 400.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:48.740
And so can we fit any more
fives into the difference?

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:50.120
So let's figure out the difference.

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:51.770
So we will subtract.

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:55.490
And just to be very clear,
this was 80 times five.

00:04:55.490 --> 00:04:56.550
The reason why we did that,

00:04:56.550 --> 00:04:59.580
you see how close did we get to 473?

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:01.500
And now we wanna figure out
how much do we have left over?

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:03.440
How many more fives can we fit in?

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:06.330
And so you subtract 400 from 473,

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:10.240
and we are going to get 73.

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:14.490
Well, we can for sure
fit more fives into 73.

00:05:14.490 --> 00:05:15.340
We might say, hey,

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:18.020
maybe let's try to fit
another 10 fives in there.

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:20.210
So let's stick another 10 fives in there.

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:21.630
Now how close are we?

00:05:21.630 --> 00:05:24.740
Well, 10 times five is 50.

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:26.600
And to be clear, what we just did here

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:30.370
is we multiplied 10 times five.

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:32.650
And now can we fit any more fives in?

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:36.970
Well, to figure that out,
we would need to subtract

00:05:36.970 --> 00:05:39.860
and figure out what we have left.

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:44.740
So 73 minus 50, that's going to be 23.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:47.950
And we can for sure
fit more fives into 23.

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:51.210
We know that five times
four is equal to 20.

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:53.810
So let's put four more fives in there.

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:56.400
So four times five is going to be 20.

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:57.960
Let's see how close we are now.

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:02.960
And to be very clear, that
is four times our five.

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:04.350
And so what do we get to?

00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:05.587
What do we have left?

00:06:05.587 --> 00:06:07.690
Can we fit any more fives in?

00:06:07.690 --> 00:06:10.370
Let's see, 23 minus 20 is just three.

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:12.120
And that's less than five,

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:15.150
so we can't fit any more
fives in, so there we have it.

00:06:15.150 --> 00:06:18.040
We were able to get 80 fives into 473.

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:19.700
We saw that we still had some left over.

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:22.330
We were able to fit another
10 into that leftover.

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:25.040
And then we still saw that
we had some left over.

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:28.410
We were able to fit another
four into that leftover.

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:29.950
And then we had a leftover of three

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:31.930
and we weren't able to
fit any more fives in.

00:06:31.930 --> 00:06:33.730
And so in total,

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:37.740
we were able to fit 94 fives

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:41.190
into 473, and then we had three left over,

00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:43.333
which is exactly what we had there.

